// Public-probe mechanism issued to composed source beside the checked standard modules.
// The transport layer (native) owns the socket mechanics: HTTPS only, no redirect, the host-configured
// byte bound and deadline, one resolution of the name whose every answer must be public, and a check of
// the peer the connection really reached; a nonpublic peer fails the read before any request is written,
// and the name's own certificate identity still authenticates the destination.
// The mechanism layer (the shipped isolate binding) owns the public-probe policy the specification
// states: the destination and authority rules, the connected-destination check, the JSON media type,
// the strict UTF-8 decode, the configured document depth and selected-character bounds, the RFC 6901
// path selection and the finite-number rule. Probes grant no application-provider reads.
// One validated read of `url`. `paths` are RFC 6901 JSON Pointers into the response document and each
// must resolve to a finite number; `asofPath` is the optional pointer to the source's own observation
// time, and an absent, unresolved, empty or nonstring value yields "" instead of a fetch time. The
// result is that validated read encoded as JSON, so composed source decodes it into its own checked type.
export function fetch(url: string, mode: string, paths: string[], asofPath: string): Promise<string>;
